WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
Parallax gives you a pregame win probability for each
NBA matchup.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.000
Let’s follow one game through the app, check the
inputs behind its forecast, and compare

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.260
that estimate with a contract price.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.320
This walkthrough uses a saved November snapshot.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.080
Start with the freshness badge.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.900
Checked tells you when the data was last refreshed.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.600
Inside a matchup, Issued tells you when that
particular forecast was saved.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.060
Open Today to browse the slate by date in Eastern
time.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.660
ESPN supplies the schedule and results.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.300
Sorting by biggest favorite shows the strongest
predicted winners.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.340
Closest forecasts brings the most evenly matched
games to the top.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.620
Let’s open Detroit at Miami.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.720
Detroit has about a 69% chance, with Miami at 31%.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.900
Across comparable games, the model would expect
Detroit to win about sixty-nine times

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.060
out of a hundred.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.040
Miami winning remains a possible result.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.920
Open Why this forecast.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.840
The breakdown follows Miami, the home team.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.480
Ratings alone put Miami at 31.9%.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.360
Home court lifts that to 36.1.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.240
Rest and travel bring it back to 30.9.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:11.220
That adjustment combines days off, estimated distance
between venues, and time-zone changes.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.500
Miami was projected to have zero days off.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:17.500
Detroit had one, alongside about 1,489 kilometers of
travel.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:22.200
In this calculation, Detroit’s extra rest outweighed
its estimated travel.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.240
These projections use the schedule available when the
forecast was issued.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.160
Team history and form adds context.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.400
The recent record uses up to ten results known at
issuance.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.400
The earlier rankings show where each team finished
previous seasons in Elo, Parallax’s

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.860
measure of relative strength.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.000
Injury coverage shows the official NBA reports
available at the cutoff.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.000
Both reports were missing for this example, so the
forecast uses its base calculation,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.900
including home court, rest, and travel.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.440
Missing coverage leaves player availability unknown.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.700
For an example with reported players, open Knicks at
Pacers.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.860
Indiana submitted a report, while New York’s coverage
was incomplete.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.760
Matched means the player’s name was connected to a
stored identity.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.750
The player-history table summarizes earlier usage and
production.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:12.190
Haliburton is listed as Out, alongside 32.4
historical minutes and zero

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.560
point six Game Score per minute.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.620
Read availability from the report status.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:21.360
Those history estimates describe what he contributed
in earlier games.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:26.860
Back in Detroit and Miami, How similar forecasts
performed compares saved forecasts in

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.760
the same probability band, using results completed
before this forecast was issued.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.200
The count tells you how much evidence supports the
comparison.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.680
Accuracy lets us examine that group more closely.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.560
First, let’s enter 60¢ for Detroit in the contract
calculator.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.640
A winning contract pays one dollar.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.140
That price requires a 60% win rate to break even
before fees.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.780
A win nets 40¢.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.000
A loss costs sixty.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.760
The model estimates a fair contract price of 69.1¢.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:02.040
At a sixty-cent purchase price, that leaves 9.1¢ of
modeled expected profit

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.280
per contract.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.840
Expected profit is an average based on the model’s
probability; a single contract can

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.980
still lose its purchase price.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.840
Now change the price to 75¢.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:17.124
Detroit is still the favorite, but the modeled
expected profit falls to minus five point

00:03:17.164 --> 00:03:17.820
nine cents.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.100
The price matters alongside the probability.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.650
This calculator uses your entered price and the saved
pregame forecast.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.020
Its figures assume settlement and exclude fees.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.180
Actual execution depends on the available market
price and liquidity.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.040
Archive pairs a saved pregame forecast with the final
score once a game finishes.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.940
Filter by season, date, or team.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.180
Here’s Golden State at Houston.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:46.703
Houston’s saved chance was about 84%, and it won one
fifteen to one oh

00:03:46.743 --> 00:03:47.000
eight.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.920
The forecast remains the estimate saved before tip.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:54.220
Older games can have a final score with no saved
forecast available.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:58.500
Teams ranks the league by Elo alongside each team’s
win-loss record.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.220
Open San Antonio to follow the rating across
completed games.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.460
Read the displayed range before judging a move.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.280
The line and game history connect those rating levels
to the results behind them.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.190
Accuracy scores each saved forecast once after the
result arrives.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.920
Winner accuracy counts how often the model’s favored
team won.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:21.840
Brier score and log loss measure probability errors,
with lower values indicating better

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:22.880
scores.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:27.040
The calibration chart asks whether teams won as often
as forecast.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.340
The diamond is the mean predicted chance.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:31.460
The circle is the observed win rate.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.460
The table below supplies the 95% intervals.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.320
In the 65–70% band, forecasts averaged 67.4%,

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.620
and favorites won 16 of 24 games, or 66.7%.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.800
Those values are close in this sample.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.920
The interval is wide because 24 games still leaves
considerable uncertainty about

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.460
the group’s win rate.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.080
Season and team filters change the sample.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.220
With all teams selected, bands follow each game’s
favorite.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:00.920
Choose Detroit, and they follow Detroit’s own chance,
including games where it was the

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:01.820
underdog.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:06.140
Its actual win rate and the model’s pick accuracy
measure different things.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.600
Results available before limits the sample to
outcomes known by a selected forecast’s

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.460
issuance.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.880
The sample filter can require ten prior games for
each team.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:20.080
Team breakdown compares actual wins with expected
wins, the sum of the selected probabilities.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:23.220
The download contains the records behind those
filters.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.680
Methodology follows the calculation from completed-
game performance through Elo, matchup

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.840
adjustments, and contract value.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.400
The sources section lists ESPN for schedules and
results, SportsDataverse for historical

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:40.140
inputs, official NBA injury reports for player
status, and GeoNames for venue coordinates.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.600
The technical paper and data downloads give you the
details behind the numbers.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:48.020
Earlier, we saw Detroit’s rating feed into its
forecast against Miami.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.840
Where did that rating come from?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.340
Start with the previous game’s box score.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:56.920
Parallax estimates possessions so it can compare
games played at different speeds.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.060
It measures scoring margin per hundred possessions,
effective field goal percentage,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:04.940
which gives threes extra credit, and true shooting
percentage, which also accounts

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.140
for free throws.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:10.400
It looks at each team’s share of offensive and
defensive rebounds, assists per turnover,

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:14.420
how often it turns the ball over, and how often it
steals the ball on an opponent’s

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.560
possession.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.500
Those eight inputs go into a weighted performance
score.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:22.340
In this fit, assists per turnover has the largest
weight among the scaled inputs,

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.160
followed by defensive rebounding.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.640
A higher assist-to-turnover ratio raises the score.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:29.080
A higher turnover rate pulls it down.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:33.420
Then Parallax compares the score with that team’s
own average from earlier games.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:36.600
A win pushes Elo up and a loss pushes it down.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.120
An upset starts with a bigger adjustment because the
result was further from what

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.500
the model expected.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.600
Three more factors shape the size.

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:47.550
First, schedule strength uses the opponent’s win
rate and the records of teams it

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.140
has faced.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:52.580
Beating a strong opponent earns more credit, and
losing to one costs less.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.580
Second, lead retention compares the final margin
with the largest lead held by either

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.420
team.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:01.600
A game that ends close after a big lead produces a
smaller multiplier than one that

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.440
ends near its widest margin.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:08.200
Third, the box-score comparison rewards a win backed
by above-usual performance and

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.100
softens the rating drop when a team plays above its
usual level in a loss.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:15.833
Between seasons, teams carry over half their
distance from the league baseline of

00:07:15.873 --> 00:07:16.500
fifteen hundred.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.260
That preserves some of what the model learned while
giving teams room to change.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.640
For the next matchup, the Elo gap sets the starting
probability.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:28.860
The fitted home-court bonus favors the home team and
drops out at a neutral venue.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.680
The model compares days off, estimated travel
distance, and time-zone changes for

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:34.960
both sides.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:40.260
Against Miami, Detroit’s extra rest outweighed its
estimated travel, bringing Miami’s

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:43.260
chance down after the home-court bump.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:48.300
When verified injury reports are available, Parallax
looks at each player’s designation,

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:51.580
expected minutes, and past Game Score per minute.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:55.380
That gives the model a way to distinguish a high-
minute contributor from a player

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.180
with a smaller role.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:01.500
It combines those inputs with the base forecast on a
log-odds scale, then converts

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.540
the result back to a probability.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.480
If neither team has verified report coverage, the
base forecast carries through.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:12.960
Detroit’s sixty-nine point one percent forecast
implies a fair contract price of

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.840
sixty-nine point one cents.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.760
At a sixty-cent buy price, the model estimates nine
point one cents of expected profit

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.280
before fees.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:26.640
The price also tells you the break-even win rate and
what you’d gain or lose at settlement.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:31.720
After the game, Archive pairs the saved pregame
forecast with the final score.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:37.280
Accuracy uses those same saved records to check
whether teams won as often as forecast.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:41.820
The notation glossaries explain the symbols, Fitted
model constants shows the values

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:46.540
selected by minimizing historical log loss, and the
technical paper and season downloads

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.460
let you trace the forecasts back to their inputs.
